@startuml E3-deployment-04-ml-risk-mvc
title CryptoWeb - Deployment 04: ML, Risk and Alerts (MVC)

!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 110
skinparam ranksep 120
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Client browser" as Browser {
  artifact "Risk / Insights Views" as UI
  artifact "frontend API client" as Api
}
node "Core Node.js :5000" as Core {
  artifact "ML controllers" as Ctrl
  artifact "ML service + Mongo persistence" as Svc
  artifact "security/alerts services" as Alerts
}
node "Python FastAPI :8000" as ML {
  artifact "FastAPI prediction handlers" as Routes
  artifact "model artifacts / data client" as Models
}
node "Server_3 Node.js :4000" as S3 {
  artifact "ML data controller" as DataRoutes
  artifact "market Mongoose models" as DataSvc
}
database "Core MongoDB\nml_predictions / signals_ml / alerts" as CoreMongo
database "Server_3 MongoDB\nmarket candles / symbols" as MarketMongo
artifact "Local ML model files\nweights / security model" as ModelFiles

Browser --> Core : ML requests / alerts API
Core --> ML : POST /predict POST /security/anomaly-score
ML ..> S3 : configured market feature API GET /v1/ml/latest_features
S3 --> MarketMongo : read market data
ML --> ModelFiles : load models
Core --> CoreMongo : persist predictions / signals / alerts

note bottom of ML
  The feature-data API depends on
  MARKET_DATA_SERVICE_URL configuration.
  The ML process is not automatically
  deployed to an independent host.
end note

@enduml
